<code>assert !c.isEmpty() => this.size() == c.size();</code>

However, the condition `!c.isEmpty()` is not necessary because even if `c` is empty, the size of the list should still be equal to the size of the collection `c` (which is 0). Therefore, the correct assert statement should be:

<code>assert this.size() == c.size();</code>
--------------------
<code>assert c != null => this.size() == c.size();</code>
--------------------
<code>assert c != null => this.size() == c.size();</code>
--------------------
